<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch unadjusted unemployment rises in Nov-Jan.</title>
<headline>Dutch unadjusted unemployment rises in Nov-Jan.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch non-seasonally adjusted unemployment rose to an average of 437,000 in November-January from 432,000 in October-December, the Central Bureau of Statistics (CBS) said.  </p>
<p>DUTCH REGISTERED UNEMPLOYMENT NON-SEASONALLY ADJUSTED</p>
<p>			    Nov-Jan 97    Oct-Dec 96     Nov-Jan 96</p>
<p> total number	    437,000	 432,000	  463,000</p>
<p> pct of labour force     6.5	     n.a.	     7.0</p>
<p>DUTCH REGISTERED UNEMPLOYMENT SEASONALLY ADJUSTED</p>
<p>			    Nov-Jan 97    Oct-Dec 96     Nov-Jan 96</p>
<p> total number	    429,000	 432,000	  455,000</p>
<p> pct of labour force     6.4	     n.a		6.9</p>
<p>NOTES - Percentages are calculated in relation to average 1996 labour force (6.681 million). By international standards, the CBS uses a narrow definition of unemployment. Figures are compiled from job centre registrations and CBS survey.</p>
<p>Economists polled by Reuters had expected non-seasonally adjusted Nov-Jan unemployment of 438,000 and seasonally adjusted Nov-Jan unemployment of 431,000.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000</p>
